WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.400
Damage the cerebellum and a person is not paralysed.

2
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.600
They move, and they move badly.

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.180
Reaches overshoot.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.380
The hand shakes as it nears the cup.

5
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.460
The cerebellum makes movements accurate, and it learns to keep them accurate.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.100
How does it learn?

7
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:19.873
Here is the circuit.

8
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:22.573
Mossy fibres excite granule cells.

9
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:27.593
Each granule cell sends an axon up to run along the fold as a parallel fibre.

10
00:00:28.633 --> 00:00:31.333
Parallel fibres pass through the dendrites of many Purkinje cells.

11
00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:35.353
Purkinje cells are the only output of the cerebellar cortex.

12
00:00:36.073 --> 00:00:40.153
They release GABA, so they inhibit the deep cerebellar nuclei.

13
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:44.593
The second input is the climbing fibre, from the inferior olive.

14
00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:47.273
Each adult Purkinje cell receives one.

15
00:00:47.893 --> 00:00:50.513
Simple spikes are ordinary action potentials.

16
00:00:50.853 --> 00:00:54.993
A complex spike is a large spike, one for each climbing fibre event.

17
00:00:55.553 --> 00:01:00.313
In a made-up recording, 130 simple spikes in 2 s is 65 Hz.

18
00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:02.873
2 complex spikes is 1 Hz.

19
00:01:03.917 --> 00:01:06.937
Marr and Albus proposed that the climbing fibre is a teacher.

20
00:01:07.537 --> 00:01:11.417
When it fires together with some parallel fibres, those synapses change.

21
00:01:12.277 --> 00:01:14.397
Ito and Kano paired the two inputs in rabbits.

22
00:01:15.277 --> 00:01:19.137
Transmission from parallel fibre to Purkinje cell was depressed for a long time.

23
00:01:19.757 --> 00:01:22.217
This is long-term depression, or LTD.

24
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:26.457
A weaker synapse means the Purkinje cell fires less in that context.

25
00:01:26.457 --> 00:01:30.717
It inhibits its nuclear target less, so the nuclear output rises.

26
00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:33.307
Try it with prism goggles.

27
00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:36.987
A made-up thrower's first throw lands 20 cm to the right.

28
00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:41.527
Each throw corrects a fixed fraction, 0.30, of the remaining error.

29
00:01:42.107 --> 00:01:46.147
The error falls to 14.0, then 9.8, then 6.86.

30
00:01:46.907 --> 00:01:49.307
After 7 corrections, it is 1.65.

31
00:01:50.047 --> 00:01:51.187
Now remove the prisms.

32
00:01:51.787 --> 00:01:55.367
The first throw lands about 18.4 cm to the left.

33
00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:57.847
The eye-hand mapping was recalibrated.

34
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.510
The teacher idea has limits.

35
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:05.410
In two monkeys, a complex spike predicted the next trial's output change during

36
00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.430
gain-increase learning of an eye reflex, but not during gain-decrease learning.

37
00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:14.870
Three mouse lines with no LTD in standard slice tests learned all three tasks

38
00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:19.690
normally, though modified protocols induced LTD in slices from two of them.

39
00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:24.070
So the teacher's effect is gated, and Marr-Albus-Ito remains a model.

40
00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.390
Keep this rule. In the model, the climbing fibre teaches by weakening synapses.
